# Concept of a “bundle”

In i18n, a bundle = collection of translated strings for a locale.

In our case: one YAML file per locale. The whole file is the “bundle.”

Example: en-US/messages.yaml maps msg.handshake.welcome → "Welcome to the Saskan Lands".

Loading the bundle = parsing that YAML into a Python dict.

Then you can look up any key in memory without re-reading the file.

Think of it like:

Bundle (YAML file) = a bag of phrases.

Key (msg.handshake.welcome) = the handle.

Value = the translated string.

So _load_bundle("es-ES") = “give me the Spanish bag of phrases as a dict.”
